            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-92-f3" n="5" xml:id="d710a-92-f3-content">
                <p>See the map facing <ref target="frus1945Berlinv01#pg_748">p. 748 in vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi></ref>. For the origin and a description
                    of the Curzon Line, see <ref
                        target="frus1919Parisv13#pg_793"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, The Paris Peace Conference, 1919, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">xiii</hi>, pp. 793</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1919Parisv13#pg_794">794</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-92-f4" n="6" xml:id="d710a-92-f4-content">
                <p>For an account of the meeting with Churchill, see Churchill, <hi rendition="#italic">Triumph and Tragedy</hi>, p. 661;
                    Rozek, <hi rendition="#italic">Allied Wartime Diplomacy</hi>, p. 408.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
